Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to Germany.\N欢迎来到德国。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.87,0:00:07.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can see you're already getting comfortable for our fireside chat.\N我看得出来你们已经为我们的轻松对话准备好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.55,0:00:12.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Also, also a bartender.\N还有，也是一位调酒师。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.27,0:00:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,But Chanza, if you could swap jobs with Jensen for just a day, what would you do first, you think?\N但默茨总理，如果你能和黄仁勋只交换一天工作，你认为你会先做什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.91,0:00:25.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's a great idea to to swap the jobs.\N哦，交换工作的想法太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.01,0:00:27.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Would you like to go there?\N你想去那里吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.79,0:00:31.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,No. Well, thank you.\N不，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.55,0:00:34.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I give you my answer.\N我给出我的答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.11,0:00:39.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,I rather would put my leather jacket on.\N我更愿意穿上我的皮夹克。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.07,0:00:41.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would take a flight to Berlin.\N我会飞往柏林。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.95,0:00:49.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would like to see the German chancellor and I would tell him I'm ready to invest.\N我想见德国总理，并告诉他我已经准备好投资了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.23,0:00:52.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, that's exactly what I'm doing.\N嗯，这正是我正在做的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.67,0:00:55.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we could arrange a meeting.\N我觉得我们可以安排一次会面。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.47,0:00:58.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, nobody has invested more in Germany.\N不，没有人比我们更投入德国了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.67,0:00:59.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for that.\N谢谢你。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.52,0:01:00.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are really grateful.\N我们非常感激。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.71,0:01:04.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for doing this and this is a great signal for our country.\N谢谢你这么做，这对我们的国家是一个非常积极的信号。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.51,0:01:05.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.07,0:01:05.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank Thank you.\N谢谢，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.02,0:01:12.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you you know uh Nvidia's story and Germany's story uh played a very large role.\N嗯，你知道，英伟达的故事和德国的故事起到了非常重要的作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.94,0:01:18.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh in fact in the year 2000 Nvidia was a consumer oriented technology.\N事实上，在2000年，英伟达还是一家面向消费者的科技公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.74,0:01:20.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were only building for PC gaming.\N当时我们只专注于个人电脑游戏领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.93,0:01:29.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it was a company in Germany, Elsa, that partners, that partnership led us into workstations, which led us into all of the car companies.\N当时德国的一家公司艾尔萨（Elsa）与我们合作，这一合作让我们进入了工作站领域，进而进入了所有汽车公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.95,0:01:39.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And today we work with the car companies from styling, design, engineering, simulation, manufacturing all the way out to the cars.\N如今，我们从汽车的设计、工程、仿真、制造，一直到最终的车辆，都与汽车公司紧密合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.30,0:01:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was in 2005 that Audi brought us into the car industry inside the car.\N2005年，奥迪将我们带入了汽车工业，就在车里。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.04,0:01:49.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it was uh 2023, was it 2023?\N那是2023年吗？是2023年吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.46,0:02:00.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,2020 uh yeah 2020 that Ola and I established a partnership to build autonomous vehicles and so Germany and video has been very close for a long time.\N2020年，是的，2020年，奥拉和我建立了合作，共同开发自动驾驶汽车，因此德国和英伟达长期以来一直保持着密切关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.35,0:02:04.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,J I think I already heard that you wouldn't like to swap jobs.\N我想我之前已经听说了，你并不想换工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.00,0:02:08.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I won't even get there asking you what you would do as a chancellor.\N所以我干脆就不问你，如果当了总理你会做什么了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.30,0:02:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We let you be you for now.\N现在我们还是让你做你自己。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:16.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I suspect you can already picture things that we might not even imagine yet.\N我猜你已经能想象出一些我们甚至还没想到的事了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.06,0:02:21.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So take us into an engineering office or a factory of the future.\N那就带我们走进一个未来的工程办公室或工厂吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.19,0:02:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you see?\N你看到了什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.96,0:02:23.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,What are this going to look like?\N它会是什么样子？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.03,0:02:25.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's interesting.\N哦，这很有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.95,0:02:32.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh in fact, the factory, every single company in the future will have two factories.\N事实上，未来的每一家公司都会有两座工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.15,0:02:35.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,The factory that is real and the factory that is digital.\N真实的工厂和数字工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.41,0:02:40.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the factory that is digital will be so real it might as be real.\N而这个数字工厂将如此真实，几乎等同于真实工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.83,0:02:50.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,if it manifests itself when you create the digital twin of your company, of your car company, that digital twin might as well be real.\N当你在创建公司或汽车公司的数字孪生体时，这个数字孪生体几乎就等同于真实存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.54,0:03:00.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so in the future, I believe that most people here in Germany will mostly work inside a digital twin of their company.\N因此，我相信未来德国这里的大多数人将主要在公司数字孪生体中工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.83,0:03:02.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,They will build digital cars.\N他们将打造数字汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.61,0:03:05.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Those cars will have digital brains.\N这些汽车将拥有数字大脑。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.23,0:03:11.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,The manufacturing the factories will have digital of course artificial intelligence\N制造工厂本身也将具备数字能力，当然还有人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.34,0:03:18.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,robots building inside a robotic factory building cars that will be robotic\N机器人在机器人工厂中建造汽车，这些汽车也将是智能化的。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.34,0:03:26.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,and everything will be completely software driven everything will be completely AIdriven so every company will build two things they will build brains\N所有事物都将完全由软件驱动，所有事物都将完全由人工智能驱动，因此每家公司都将打造两样东西：它们将打造大脑。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.15,0:03:33.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the brains that go into uh the products that they that they ship and so fascinating yeah it's going to be cool\N以及这些大脑将被嵌入到他们交付的产品中，这非常有趣，是的，这将非常酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.15,0:03:44.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,chanc of course the ambition is to bring AI into everyday use across German industry from large manufacturers Middleton to also smaller firms.\N总理当然，我们的目标是将人工智能带入德国工业的日常应用，从大型制造商到中小企业。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.10,0:03:47.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could you perhaps share a few concrete examples of how you and the\N你能分享一些具体例子吗，关于你和德国
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.50,0:03:54.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,German government are ensuring that this widespread uh deployment is actually taking place?\N德国政府正在确保这种广泛部署真正得以实施吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.43,0:03:54.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sure.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.77,0:04:04.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,First of all, I would like to say that I'm really impressed what um Nvidia and German companies are already doing in this country.\N首先，我想说，我对英伟达以及德国企业目前在本国所做的一切真的印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.07,0:04:09.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Ola Kelenius just handed out a model from the new S-Class of Mercedes to me.\N奥拉·凯伦纽斯刚刚把一辆新款梅赛德斯S级轿车的模型送给了我。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.96,0:04:18.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh promising that this car will be autonomous driving in Germany by the end of this year.\N他承诺，这辆车将在今年年底前实现德国境内的自动驾驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.59,0:04:20.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safest and the most autonomous.\N最安全且最智能的自动驾驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.99,0:04:28.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is happening in Germany.\N所以这正在德国发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.11,0:04:30.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we are in the government.\N所以我们身在政府。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.50,0:04:37.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are fully committed to be one of the most advanced places in the world,\N我们完全致力于成为全球最先进地区之一，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.71,0:04:45.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,not just in the European Union, but in the world to work with EI, AI, to integrate AI into our industry.\N不仅在欧盟，更在全球范围内，推动人工智能发展，将人工智能融入我们的工业。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.46,0:04:51.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one of the biggest, if not the biggest advantage we have in Germany is our so-called middle.\N我们在德国最大的优势之一，或许就是所谓的中小企业。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.87,0:05:00.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm very happy to see that we are having here tonight many smaller and mediumsized companies from Germany.\N我非常高兴今晚能看到这么多德国的中小型企业在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.27,0:05:09.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Please open your doors for AI to make use of your data.\N请打开你们的大门，让人工智能利用你们的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.47,0:05:12.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is so decisive for the German future.\N这对德国的未来至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.94,0:05:19.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a real secret and a real advantage for Germany to use\N这是德国真正隐藏的秘诀，也是真正的优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.12,0:05:25.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,to make use of all the data which are already available in our companies.\N充分利用我们企业中已有的所有数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.60,0:05:33.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if we could combine this AI with companies like yours and our companies in Germany, the big ones,\N如果我们能将人工智能与你们这样的企业以及德国的大型企业结合，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.49,0:05:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also the so-called middle, I'm really optimistic that we will be one of the leading,\N以及所谓的中小企业，我非常乐观，我们将成为全球领先，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.08,0:05:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,if not the leading country in the world in terms of spread AI for all the companies of our manufacturers,\N甚至可能是世界上在推广人工智能应用于所有制造商、
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.68,0:05:54.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,machinery, automotive industry, suppliers of automotive industry.\N机械、汽车工业及汽车供应商方面的领先国家。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.48,0:05:58.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think this is a great opportunity and I'm delighted to meet that.\N我认为这是一个绝佳的机会，我很高兴能参与其中。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.59,0:06:03.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you're absolutely right.\N是的，你说得完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.71,0:06:09.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So So, so first of all,\N所以，首先，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.07,0:06:16.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,the data of Germany is part of your natural resources.\N德国的数据是你们的自然资源的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.07,0:06:18.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It belongs to the nation.\N它属于国家。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.14,0:06:23.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,The data of your the the digital experience or otherwise known as data.\N你的数字体验数据，也就是数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.63,0:06:32.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,The data of your country is your culture, your values, your knowledge, your experience.\N你国家的数据就是你的文化、价值观、知识和经验。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.51,0:06:33.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's your natural resource.\N它是你的自然资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.89,0:06:37.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,It belongs to the nation.\N它属于国家。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.08,0:06:48.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you're absolutely right that you should import the technology to harvest that data and turn it into your national intelligence.\N你说得完全正确，你应该引进技术来采集这些数据，并将其转化为国家智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.27,0:06:54.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you should not export your culture, export your values, export your knowledge,\N但你不应该输出你的文化、输出你的价值观、输出你的知识，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.99,0:07:00.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,export your history, and then import German intelligence back.\N输出你的历史，然后再引进德国的智能回来。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.39,0:07:01.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Makes no sense.\N这毫无意义。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.54,0:07:02.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's number one.\N所以这是第一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.99,0:07:10.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you you out of you you have every you're going to of course use the best AI technology\N因此，你当然会使用世界上最好的人工智能技术和全球的人工智能服务，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.05,0:07:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,available in the world and AI services in the world but you have every capability to build your own AI.\N但你完全有能力自主构建自己的人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.16,0:07:18.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's number one.\N这是第一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.44,0:07:23.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second is the next wave of AI is physical AI.\N第二点是，下一波人工智能将是实体人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.91,0:07:27.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where AI interacts with the physical world.\N这是指人工智能与物理世界进行交互。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.42,0:07:37.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,robotics, manufacturing, cars, heavy industry that will never be replaced by digital technology.\N机器人、制造、汽车、重工业，这些领域永远无法被数字技术取代。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.03,0:07:45.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,The work that you know belongs that knowledge belongs to you.\N你所熟知的工作，相关的知识属于你。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.63,0:07:50.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,The expertise of your domain that belongs to you.\N你所在领域的专业技能，也属于你。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.44,0:07:56.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Artificial general intelligence will never replace domain expertise.\N通用人工智能永远无法取代专业领域的知识。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.97,0:08:01.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could be as smart of a general intelligence as you want.\N无论你拥有多么聪明的通用人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.15,0:08:11.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You will never be as smart as somebody who is very very specialized in a particular field of electro mechanical technology.\N你永远无法比得上一个在机电技术某个特定领域极其专精的人。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.04,0:08:13.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It cannot be replaced.\N这是无法被取代的。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.79,0:08:16.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so AI can only augment your capability.\N因此，人工智能只能增强你的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.84,0:08:18.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will not replace your capability.\N它不会取代你的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.88,0:08:22.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So take advantage of the technology.\N所以要充分利用这项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.19,0:08:28.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a new instrument.\N这是一项新工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.59,0:08:35.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,As for some of these advantages, um Jensen, we have on the one hand decades of industrial data.\N至于这些优势，黄仁勋，一方面我们拥有数十年的工业数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.98,0:08:39.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have very um skilled labor if you like.\N我们拥有非常熟练的劳动力，如果你愿意这么说的话。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.62,0:08:42.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have the engineering expertise.\N我们具备工程专长。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.65,0:08:48.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so this certainly as um you seem to point out uh speaks for a lot of advantages for Germany.\N因此，正如你似乎指出的那样，这显然凸显了德国的诸多优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.74,0:08:50.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have a global perspective.\N你拥有全球视野。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.35,0:08:55.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, there are other countries that also have strengths that also like to take advantage of their strengths.\N然而，其他国家也具备自身优势，并且同样希望利用这些优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.51,0:08:59.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,You talk to so many governments across the globe to so many companies across the world.\N你与全球各地的政府、世界各地的公司都有交流。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.87,0:09:04.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you take this global perspective,\N如果你从全球视角来看，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.59,0:09:13.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,how is Germany braced for this sort of next race in AI?\N德国如何为这场人工智能的下一轮竞赛做好准备？
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.15,0:09:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you know, the last major industrial revolution was electrification before the one I'll describe.\N如你所知，上一次重大的工业革命是电气化，而我接下来要描述的是下一次。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.51,0:09:32.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Electrification resulted in really three geographical leaders,\N电气化催生了三个地理上的领先者，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.27,0:09:35.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Germany, United States, Japan.\N德国、美国和日本。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.95,0:09:45.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,For the last 50 years, because of the current industrial revolution, which is computing and digital technology,\N在过去50年里，由于当前这场工业革命——即计算和数字技术，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.95,0:09:55.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,United States has largely exported its heavy manufacturing, its building, its craft really to China.\N美国已将重工业、建筑业和手工艺制造大量转移到中国。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.91,0:10:05.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now the world has three again, but it's Germany, Japan, and China.\N如今世界再次形成三足鼎立，但这次是德国、日本和中国。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.07,0:10:12.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,The advantage that China has is that they came into their industrial revolution, if you will,\N中国的优势在于，它们的工业革命（如果可以这么称呼的话），
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.11,0:10:19.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,their economic transformation happened during precisely the time of the computer industry.\N其经济转型恰好发生在全球计算机产业兴起的时期。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.63,0:10:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,They are quite computerized.\N中国的工业化程度非常高。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.51,0:10:34.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,China is probably the only nation today that is deep in manufacturing and deep in computer science and very comfortable in both.\N今天，中国可能是唯一一个在制造业和计算机科学两个领域都深入发展且都游刃有余的国家。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.27,0:10:38.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, the good news is there's a complete reset.\N好消息是，现在迎来了全面重启。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.99,0:10:42.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,The last 50 years was about software programming.\N过去50年，核心是软件编程。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.82,0:10:47.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,United States is obviously world class.\N美国显然处于世界顶尖水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.47,0:10:49.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's a new era now.\N但现在是一个新时代。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.36,0:10:52.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,The computer programs itself.\N计算机可以自我编程。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.67,0:10:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,You just have to show the computer what you want.\N你只需要告诉计算机你想要什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.27,0:11:06.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Computer programming all of the advantages of the last generation has now been acred into artificial intelligence.\N上一代的所有优势现在已被整合进人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.83,0:11:10.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a complete reset.\N这是一次彻底的重启。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.51,0:11:18.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,All the digital technology in the world will not replace electro mechanical physical technology.\N世界上所有的数字技术都无法取代机电物理技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.35,0:11:23.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Electrons will never replace atoms.\N电子永远无法取代原子。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.07,0:11:25.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's an advantage that you have.\N这正是你的优势所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.95,0:11:33.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,The work you know, the domain expertise you have, the craft that is here, it will remain here.\N你所熟知的工作，你拥有的专业领域知识，以及这里的工艺技能，都将长久保留。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.77,0:11:36.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you have to take advantage of this new technology.\N但你必须利用这项新技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.67,0:11:41.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,This in this industrial revolution is so mighty, is so powerful.\N这次工业革命如此强大，如此势不可挡。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.63,0:11:51.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't have another chance because you've always Yeah.\N你不会再有另一个机会，因为你一直都在。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.39,0:11:56.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whether we have another chance or not, we should always assume we don't.\N无论我们是否还有机会，都应始终假设没有。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.11,0:11:59.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,This transition is so important.\N这次转型至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.47,0:12:07.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,You should combine your deep skills, your deep expertise in the physical products,\N你应该结合你在实体产品方面的深厚技能和专业知识，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.38,0:12:13.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the electromechanical products and combine it with artificial intelligence.\N以及在机电产品方面的专长，并与人工智能相结合。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.53,0:12:24.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would not be surprised if currently most of the mishads their challenges are reduction in labor because people are getting old.\N如果目前他们面临的大多数挑战都源于劳动力减少，因为人们正在变老，我不会感到惊讶。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.35,0:12:31.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,The craft of that is captured in the knowledge the skills of\N这种技艺体现在人们的知识和技能中，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.06,0:12:36.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,the people are still are starting to get older and older every generation.\N而这些人才正一代代变得越来越年长。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.38,0:12:38.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take advantage of artificial intelligence.\N充分利用人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.78,0:12:39.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let them codify.\N让它们将知识编码化。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.95,0:12:41.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let them program.\N让它们进行编程。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.57,0:12:46.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let them teach this artificial intelligence and keep it here in Germany, right?\N让它们学习并训练这种人工智能，让它留在德国，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.43,0:12:54.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And let it re-engineer the chancellor's words, chancellor's words, re-engineer Germany.\N并让它重新设计总理的言论，重新设计德国。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.19,0:12:56.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is your chance to do it.\N这是你们实现目标的机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.99,0:13:01.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.63,0:13:07.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's become obvious prerequisites to scale industrial AI in Germany um are\N我认为在德国规模化工业人工智能的必要前提已经具备，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.03,0:13:13.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,here and they are very promising and the opportunities related to it are impressive.\N这些前提非常有前景，相关机遇令人印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.41,0:13:23.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,It will be key of course Chancellor to bridge the gap between innovation and implementation in factories and in value chains.\N总理，当然关键在于弥合工厂和价值链中创新与实施之间的差距。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.31,0:13:30.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is a cooperation with Nvidia a part of the plan to do so?\N与英伟达的合作是否也是实现这一目标的计划之一？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.83,0:13:31.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, sure.\N当然，没问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.46,0:13:33.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is already happening.\N而且这已经正在发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.20,0:13:44.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I would like to say that I'm extremely grateful about what we have just heard from um this this business leader of the world in terms of AI.\N我想说，我非常感激刚才这位全球人工智能领域的企业领袖所分享的内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.59,0:13:53.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you are giving me and hopefully us a great optimism about our business model in Germany.\N所以您让我，也让我们所有人，对德国的商业模式充满极大的信心。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.67,0:14:04.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you might know that I am always insisting that we have to remain a country with manufacturing and we\N你们可能知道，我一直强调我们必须保持一个制造业国家的身份，我们
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.55,0:14:14.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,should never give up that and now we are seeing a great opportunity in combining our experiences with manufacturing and AI.\N永远不应放弃这一点，而现在我们看到了一个绝佳机会，将我们的制造业经验与人工智能相结合。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.61,0:14:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if we are successful in bringing these two aspects and parts of the business of the future together,\N所以如果我们能成功地将这两方面、这两个未来业务的组成部分整合在一起，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.00,0:14:29.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm really very optimistic that Germany can be one of the most successful economies in\N我非常乐观地认为，德国可以成为世界上最具成功性的经济体之一，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.82,0:14:36.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,the world because we are already we are still the third biggest economy in the world.\N因为我们目前仍是全球第三大经济体。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.30,0:14:43.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,So thank you for for for telling us what the opportunity is and comparing us with others.\N所以感谢您向我们说明了这一机遇，并将我们与其他国家进行比较。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.22,0:14:48.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I believe and I I I I share your view that the Americans made a big mistake\N我相信，我也完全认同您的观点，美国人犯了一个重大错误，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.63,0:14:57.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,to export their manufacturing and now they are faced with a very small successful but very smallbased industry.\N他们将制造业外迁，如今却面临一个规模虽小但成功的企业群体。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.01,0:15:05.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is our advantage to have this broader access and broader approach to the future of our industry.\N而这正是我们的优势所在——我们能更广泛地接触并更全面地把握我们产业的未来。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.78,0:15:14.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And look, um, I'm I'm a large American company and, um, and we, uh, have incredible partnerships here in Germany for good reason.\N顺便说一句，我来自一家大型美国公司，我们在这里与德国建立了令人难以置信的合作伙伴关系，这绝非偶然。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.14,0:15:15.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's good for us.\N这对我们有利。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.31,0:15:17.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's good for us.\N这对我们有利。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.08,0:15:21.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, our partnership with Audi led to our partnership with Mercedes.\N我们与奥迪的合作，促成了我们与梅赛德斯的合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.28,0:15:28.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our partnership with Mercedes led to our investment in robotics, which led to our partnership with Agile Robots.\N我们与梅赛德斯的合作，推动了我们在机器人领域的投资，进而促成了我们与敏捷机器人公司的合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.34,0:15:30.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just made an investment in them.\N我们刚刚对他们进行了投资。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.19,0:15:40.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we made investment uh Ailios made an investment in uh Murilla uh made an investment in um uh uh reflex aerospace.\N嗯，我们进行了投资，Ailios对Murilla进行了投资，Murilla又对Reflex Aerospace进行了投资。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.90,0:15:45.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh last year we made an investment in Black Forest Labs.\N去年我们对Black Forest Labs进行了投资。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.19,0:15:51.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh here in Germany you have deep science and technology and deep science and\N在德国，你们拥有深厚的技术和科学基础，以及深厚的科学和数学基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.38,0:15:57.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,math which are the fundamentals for manufacturing for the deep sciences for artificial intelligence.\N这些是制造业、深科技以及人工智能的根本。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.39,0:16:03.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so there's so much there's so much technical expertise and there's so much deep science and deep math.\N因此，这里拥有大量技术专长，以及大量深厚的科学和数学知识。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.61,0:16:12.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,The one thing that you said also is that you believed in a policy of advancing and encouraging AI startups or startups in general.\N你提到的另一点是，你相信应推动并鼓励人工智能初创企业或初创企业整体发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.52,0:16:13.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's fantastic.\N我认为这太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.04,0:16:19.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of the things that I really love about the United States, of course, is that we constantly reinvigorate.\N我非常欣赏美国的一点是，我们始终能够不断焕发活力。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.22,0:16:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We constantly reinvent ourselves.\N我们始终在不断自我革新。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.08,0:16:24.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the way we do that is through all the entrepreneurs.\N而我们实现这一点的方式，正是通过所有企业家。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.27,0:16:29.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so one of the things that I really love to see, we've invested tremendously in Germany.\N因此，我非常乐于看到，我们已在德国投入了大量资金。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.29,0:16:33.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the last year, we've invested almost a billion dollars.\N去年，我们投入了近十亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.28,0:16:36.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,This week, we're investing in four new companies.\N本周，我们将投资四家新公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.58,0:16:39.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, in a lot of ways,\N因此，在许多方面，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.39,0:16:49.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,we are one of the largest VCs in Germany because I believe in Germany.\N我们是德国最大的风险投资机构之一，因为我相信德国。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.05,0:16:59.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so for all of the other venture capitalists, you better hurry because otherwise I'm going to take all the good deals and I'm going to be rich.\N所以各位其他风险投资家们，你们最好快点行动，否则我就会把所有好项目都拿走，然后变得富有。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.03,0:17:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and so the the important thing is is the the thing I want\N因此，最重要的是，我想强调的是
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.97,0:17:09.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,to recognize is that the science and technology capability of Germany is just second to none.\N德国的科技实力是首屈一指的。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.56,0:17:11.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a thousand employees here.\N我们这里有上千名员工。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.32,0:17:13.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a fantastic office here in Berlin.\N我们在柏林拥有一个极棒的办公室。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.69,0:17:19.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some of the fundamental inventions of our companies came from our office here in Berlin and Germany.\N我们公司的一些基础性发明，就诞生于柏林和德国的这个办公室。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.27,0:17:22.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is you want to invest here.\N所以，你们应该在这里投资。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.17,0:17:23.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredible people.\N令人惊叹的人才。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.77,0:17:25.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,May I ask a question?\N我可以问一个问题吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.45,0:17:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could you give us an advice on regulation?\N您能给我们一些关于监管的建议吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.08,0:17:35.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are having a very strong debate in Brussels on the European level compared to the US.\N相比美国，我们在布鲁塞尔就欧洲层面的监管展开了非常激烈的讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.51,0:17:41.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,What is the best way to regulate this industry or this new technology?\N规范这一行业或这项新技术的最佳方式是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.15,0:17:46.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we agree on no regulation is not the right answer.\N我认为，不加监管显然不是正确答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.91,0:17:51.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Too tight regulation is not the right answer either.\N过于严苛的监管同样也不是正确答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.71,0:17:58.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,But what is from your view the right answer in terms of keeping\N但从您的角度来看，正确的答案是什么，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.38,0:18:04.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,the potential damage in mind that this could happen and it already happened.\N在考虑到这种潜在损害已经发生且可能再次发生的情况下。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.37,0:18:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what is your advice on on regulation?\N那么您对监管有什么建议？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.72,0:18:09.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,What can we do better than others?\N我们能做些什么，比别人做得更好？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.15,0:18:11.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safety is paramount.\N安全是首要原则。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.39,0:18:21.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, there is no future for this industry without safe products just as there's no future in autonomous vehicles if the vehicles are not safe.\N是的，如果没有安全的产品，这个行业就没有未来，正如自动驾驶汽车若不安全，也毫无未来可言。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.14,0:18:23.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it is not a choice.\N因此这不是一个选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.05,0:18:26.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't choose between safety and capability.\N你不必在安全性和能力之间做选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.43,0:18:27.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,They are one.\N它们是一体的。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.55,0:18:30.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have to go together.\N它们必须同时具备。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.06,0:18:32.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so three pillars.\N所以是三大支柱。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.24,0:18:38.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first is you can't regulate if there's no technology.\N首先，如果没有技术，就无法进行监管。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.91,0:18:43.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the technology industry must Yeah.\N因此，科技行业必须做到。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.03,0:18:49.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The technology industry must invent the technology for safety.\N科技行业必须发明安全所需的技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.12,0:18:55.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just as Ola and I had to invent the technology and we have the safest autonomous vehicle in the car in the world.\N就像奥拉和我必须发明技术，才拥有了世界上安全性最高的自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.90,0:19:01.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had to invent the technology that allows you to achieve the functionality you want to see\N我们必须发明技术，以实现你想要的功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.73,0:19:07.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also the guarantee of functional safety and active safety we want to we want to deliver.\N同时确保功能安全和主动安全，这是我们希望交付的保障。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.72,0:19:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that requires invention of technology.\N因此，这需要技术创新。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.76,0:19:12.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's the first pillar.\N这是第一个支柱。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.11,0:19:14.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,But that's something that Germany is incredibly good at.\N但这一点正是德国非常擅长的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.66,0:19:18.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Your science, your math, your technology is incredibly good.\N你们的科学、数学和技术都非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.23,0:19:21.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to invent the technology of safety.\N你们必须发明安全技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.05,0:19:23.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safety is not hopes and dreams.\N安全不是靠希望和梦想。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.41,0:19:26.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safety is technology and engineering.\N安全是技术和工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.64,0:19:31.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Second, the companies need to have best practices.\N第二，企业需要遵循最佳实践。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.55,0:19:38.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sometimes the the young companies they're still trying to grow up and they make maybe more mistakes than they should.\N有时这些初创公司仍在成长过程中，可能犯的错误比应有的要多。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.62,0:19:45.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we need to make sure that companies make deliver on the best practices,\N我们必须确保企业真正落实最佳实践。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.26,0:19:51.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,best methods and even in safety as many of the people in the audience there are probably many in the automotive industry.\N最佳方法，甚至在安全方面，现场很多观众可能来自汽车工业。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.65,0:19:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know that safety is deep methodology, deep best practices,\N你们知道，安全是一种深入的方法论，深入的最佳实践。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.04,0:20:02.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,deep engineering and that methodology has to be adhered to and then lastly\N深入的工程，而这些方法论必须得到遵守，最后是
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.54,0:20:10.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's industrial and government regulations if it turns out that and remember AI is\N如果发现人工智能存在工业和政府监管问题，记住人工智能本身
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.38,0:20:16.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,two things just as the internet regulating the internet is hard but regulating\N有两件事：正如互联网监管互联网很困难，但监管
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.43,0:20:22.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,internet applications is not so hard we should be regulating the applications right way.\N互联网应用并不那么困难，我们应该立即开始监管这些应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.10,0:20:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, uh, if there are AI technologies, um,\N所以，呃，如果存在人工智能技术，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.76,0:20:33.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,that you see that's being applied to a new type of product that is not covered by the existing regulatory bodies,\N你看到它们被应用于现有监管机构未覆盖的新类型产品，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.10,0:20:39.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,they have to re they have to evaluate as soon as possible and make sure that they their regulation includes AI.\N他们就必须尽快重新评估，并确保其监管范围涵盖人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.27,0:20:48.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I would and I I think I've also heard you say that you want to find that balance between innovation and regulation.\N所以，我认为，我也听你说过，你希望在创新与监管之间找到平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.51,0:20:52.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's nothing to regulate if the industry doesn't thrive.\N如果产业无法蓬勃发展，那就没有什么可监管的。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.91,0:20:59.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,You want the German AI industry to thrive as well as do it safely, responsibly.\N你希望德国的人工智能产业也能蓬勃发展，同时确保安全、负责任。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.95,0:21:02.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think I think the balance is really important to do.\N所以我认为，这种平衡真的非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.66,0:21:10.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think that the answer is we know there's technology we can invent and deploy in order to have AI safety.\N所以我认为，答案是：我们知道有技术可以发明和部署，以确保人工智能安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.43,0:21:15.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,We know that there are best practices that we can adhere to as companies and industries.\N我们也知道，企业与行业可以遵循的最佳实践。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.14,0:21:20.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then in addition to that if necessary we'll make sure we regulate.\N此外，如有必要，我们一定会确保进行监管。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.43,0:21:25.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just briefly chancer what would be your answer to the same question maybe very briefly.\N简短地问一下，您对这个问题的回答会是什么？可能非常简短地回答一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.55,0:21:32.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,No thank you this was extremely helpful because we we are talking about that on the European level we are talking that on the national level and my\N不用了，谢谢，这非常有帮助，因为我们正在欧洲层面讨论这个问题，也在国家层面讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.55,0:21:36.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,my approach is that we at least need the European level and better we\N我的观点是，至少我们需要欧洲层面的监管，如果可能的话，最好有全球层面的监管。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.78,0:21:44.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,had a global level of regulation and of safety for this fantastic new technology.\N为这项非凡的新技术建立全球性的监管和安全标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.40,0:21:48.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is my personal view but we we are still far from that\N这是我的个人看法，但我们离这个目标还很远。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.92,0:21:53.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we are different having a different approach between the Americans and the Europeans.\N因为我们美欧双方在方法上存在差异。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.47,0:21:55.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we are working on that.\N但我们正在努力推进。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.17,0:22:05.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And most in this room know that um I was successful to get the AI regulation out of the normal regulation of AI in the\N在座的大多数人都知道，我成功地将人工智能监管从欧盟的常规AI监管中独立出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.33,0:22:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,European Union and to have a special regulation for the machinery industry in\N为德国的机械行业制定了专门的监管规定，使其不被纳入通用AI限制和监管范围。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.52,0:22:14.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Germany and not part being part of the general AI limitation and regulation.\N这是一项重大成就，我们取得了这一成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.89,0:22:17.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this was a big achievement which we had.\N这是我们取得的一项重大成就。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.23,0:22:18.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Give Germany a chance.\N给德国一次机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.59,0:22:19.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.31,0:22:22.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Give this industry a chance to Yeah.\N给这个产业一个机会吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.27,0:22:33.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just finally, very very briefly, Chancellor, if Jensen came back in a year's time, which we very much hope, what would you hope for him to see?\N最后再简单问一句，总理，如果黄仁勋一年后回来，我们非常希望他能回来，您希望他看到什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.71,0:22:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would like to see him regularly um let's say at least once a year and discussing progresses we\N我想定期见到他，比如说每年至少一次，讨论一下进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.20,0:22:51.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,made and seeing um a guy sitting in my office and being extremely happy about the German investment place.\N看到有个家伙坐在我的办公室里，对德国的投资环境感到非常高兴。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.31,0:23:00.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nothing would give me more joy than to see all of my investments in Germany turned into gold.\N没有什么能比看到我在德国的所有投资都变成黄金更让我高兴了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.43,0:23:00.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.81,0:23:10.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I have every I have every belief and I'm very very happy to hear uh your personal support of the startup ecosystem.\N因此，我完全相信，听到您对初创企业生态系统的个人支持，我感到非常非常高兴。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.97,0:23:16.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm very happy to hear that that there are regulations involved to uh make it possible\N我很高兴听到，原来有相关规定，才能实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.98,0:23:23.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,for the pension funds and the and the risk capital the risk capital to come into Germany.\N对于养老基金和风险资本而言，风险资本将流入德国。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.39,0:23:28.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then and then I'm I'm also I'm also uh super excited to hear about all\N然后，我同样非常期待听到所有这些内容
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.22,0:23:32.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the AI startups and the startups that have happened in the last couple of years.\N人工智能初创企业以及过去几年间涌现的初创企业。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.11,0:23:37.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Half of the startups in Germany being founded in the last two years is AI.\N德国一半的初创企业是在过去两年内成立的，且都与人工智能相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.87,0:23:38.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's terrific.\N是的，这太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.92,0:23:39.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's oriented.\N这很有方向感。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.96,0:23:43.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's who knows maybe you are going to ask them for some autographs next year.\N是啊，说不定明年你还要向他们索要签名呢。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.86,0:23:49.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,You might want to pin a bring a pen when you come once they have their breakthroughs.\N你来的时候最好带上一支笔，等他们取得突破时可以签名留念。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.47,0:23:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some of them uh I understand were your interns uh in the past and now they run their own companies.\N我听说其中一些人过去曾是你的实习生，现在他们自己创办了公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.40,0:23:58.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's been a pleasure to have you here.\N很高兴你们能来。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.18,0:23:59.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you to both of you.\N谢谢你们两位。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.42,0:24:07.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ladies and gentlemen, please give a thank you an applause to Chancellor Mer and Jensen W.\N各位女士先生，请用掌声感谢默茨总理和黄仁勋。
